,"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-11-12","period":"2026-09-27","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/829224/000082922426000162/sbux-20260927.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"In this Annual Report on Form 10-K (\"10-K\" or \"Report\") for the fiscal year ended September 27, 2026 (\"fiscal 2026\"), Starbucks Corporation (together with its subsidiaries) is referred to as \"Starbucks,\" the \"Company,\" \"we,\" \"us,\" or \"our.\"","zh":null},{"en":"Starbucks is the premier roaster, marketer, and retailer of specialty coffee in the world, operating in 91 markets. Formed in 1985, Starbucks Corporation's common stock trades on the Nasdaq Global Select Market (\"Nasdaq\") under the symbol \"SBUX.\" We purchase and roast high-quality coffees that we sell, along with handcrafted coffee, tea, and other beverages and a variety of high-quality food items through company-operated coffeehouses (previously referred to as \"stores\"). We also sell a variety of coffee and tea products and license our trademarks through other channels, such as licensed coffeehouses as well as grocery and foodservice through our Global Coffee Alliance with Nestl S.A. (\"Nestl \"). In addition to our flagship Starbucks Coffee brand, we sell goods and services under the following brands: Teavana , Ethos , and Starbucks Reserve .","zh":null},{"en":"Our primary objective is to maintain Starbucks standing as one of the most recognized and respected brands in the world. We believe the continuous investments in our brand and operations will deliver long-term targeted revenue and income growth. This includes expansion of our global coffeehouse base, adding coffeehouses in both existing, developed markets such as the U.S. and in higher growth markets, as well as optimizing the mix of company-operated and licensed coffeehouses around the world. In addition, by leveraging experiences gained through our coffeehouses and elsewhere, we continue to drive beverage, equipment, process, and technology innovation, including in our industry-leading digital platform. We strive to regularly offer consumers new, innovative coffee and other products in a variety of forms, across new categories and diverse channels.","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[{"en":"Revenue from company-operated coffeehouses accounted for 82% of total net revenues during fiscal 2026, which includes the impact of converting Starbucks retail operations in China from company-operated to licensed coffeehouses in the third quarter of fiscal 2026. Our retail objective is to be the leading retailer and brand of coffee and tea in each of our target markets by selling the finest quality coffee, tea, and related products, as well as complementary food offerings, and by providing each customer with a unique Starbucks Experience. The Starbucks Experience is built upon superior customer service through the Green Apron Service model, convenience, and a seamless digital experience as well as warm and welcoming coffeehouses that reflect the personalities of the communities in which they operate, thereby building a high degree of customer loyalty.","zh":null}],"competition":[{"en":"Our primary competitors for coffee beverage sales are specialty coffee retailers and shops. We believe that our customers choose among specialty coffee retailers and shops primarily on the basis of product quality, brand reputation, service, experience, and convenience, as well as price. We continue to experience direct competition from large competitors in the quick-service restaurant sector and the ready-to-drink coffee beverage market, in addition to both well-established and start-up companies in many international markets. We also compete with restaurants and other specialty retailers for prime retail locations and qualified personnel to operate both new and existing coffeehouses.","zh":null},{"en":"Our coffee and tea products sold through our Channel Development segment compete directly against specialty coffees and teas sold through grocery stores, warehouse clubs, specialty retailers, convenience stores, and foodservice accounts and also compete indirectly against all other coffees and teas on the market.","zh":null}],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2026-09-27","items":[{"name":"North America","val":28897800000,"zh":"North America"},{"name":"International","val":6744400000,"zh":"國際"},{"name":"Channel Development","val":2172700000,"zh":"Channel Development"}],"total":37910600000},"prod":{"end":"2026-09-27","items":[{"name":"Company Operated Coffeehouses","val":30940200000,"zh":"Company Operated Coffeehouses"},{"name":"Beverage","val":22413900000,"zh":"Beverage"},{"name":"Other Products","val":8089000000,"zh":"Other Products"},{"name":"Food","val":7407700000,"zh":"Food"},{"name":"Licensed Coffeehouses","val":4615800000,"zh":"Licensed Coffeehouses"},{"name":"Product & Service Other","val":2354600000,"zh":"Product & Service Other"}],"total":37910600000},"geo":{"end":"2026-09-27","items":[{"name":"US","val":28791900000,"zh":"美國"},{"name":"Other Countries","val":7338000000,"zh":"其他國家"},{"name":"CN","val":1780700000,"zh":"中國"}],"total":37910600000}},"peers":["NKE","COST","DIS","V","WMT"]}}